# Copy to `.env` and point at an API the phone can actually reach.
#
# `localhost` is the phone itself, not this machine. On a physical device use the
# development machine's LAN address; on the Android emulator use 10.0.2.2, which
# is its alias for the host loopback.
#
#   physical device   http://192.168.1.23:3000
#   Android emulator  http://10.0.2.2:3000
#   deployed API      https://saulado-api.onrender.com
#
# Expo inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_* at build time, so a running Metro will not pick up a
# change here — restart it. The value ships inside the app and anyone can read it
# out of the bundle, which is why no secret may ever carry this prefix.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.0.2.2:3000

# The web app's public origin — the same value the backend has as `APP_URL`,
# because that is what it builds password-reset and email-confirm links from.
#
# `app.config.ts` reads this to decide which host the app claims for universal
# links (iOS `applinks:`, Android verified intent filters). Only an `https` value
# is used; anything else leaves those out, since neither platform verifies a link
# over plain HTTP. Deep links still work in development through the `saulado://`
# scheme, which needs no domain at all.
EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://saulado.example.com
